  "pairing": "garamond-karla",
  "typeCharacter": "EB Garamond brings a Viennese, old-shop elegance. It is set very large (h1 about 9 to 11vw, regular weight, sentence case, tight leading) and in medium sizes for section heads. Karla handles running text, service names and hours in small, plain sentence-case sizes, with medium weight for service names.",
  "composition": "Hero on deep green-black #14201d. Columns 1 to 7: the h1 in huge Garamond in #eeeae3, broken over three lines, then the lead in Karla at 6 columns in #9fb0ad and a single oxblood #b23a2e rectangular button with slightly square corners. Columns 8 to 12: a large pale steel line drawing of an open straight razor, angled diagonally and bleeding off the right edge, with three thin curls of steam above it. A slim top bar carries the wordmark 'Brivnica Kos' in Garamond at left and the phone at right. Next comes a full-width oxblood #b23a2e ribbon with a single line of short words in Garamond #f6f2ec separated by small diamonds: Zagreb, Dunaj, Maribor, Poštna ulica. The story section follows on light tint #eef1f0 with ink #14201d: the heading at columns 1 to 5 and the text at columns 6 to 11, with a small ink drawing of a folded hot towel at columns 1 to 4 under the heading. The services section returns to dark #14201d: the heading at columns 1 to 4, and at columns 5 to 12 a long ruled list of the six offerings, with each name in Garamond, a Karla note where one exists, #2f413c hairline rules between them, and the note about boys' prices at the end. The booking section is a full oxblood band: the heading and text at columns 1 to 6, and the phone as a giant Garamond numeral in #f6f2ec at columns 7 to 12. The contact section on surface #1c2b27 has the address at columns 1 to 4, the opening hours as a week strip at columns 5 to 8, and a schematic line map of the old-town streets at columns 9 to 12, with Poštna ulica marked by a small oxblood dot.",
  "imagery": "No photographs at all. All art is ink line drawing. The hero shows an open straight razor with steam curls in thin pale steel #9fb0ad and #eeeae3 lines on plain #14201d. The story section shows a small folded hot towel drawn in #14201d ink on plain #eef1f0. The contact section has a simple schematic street map in thin lines. None of the art contains letters, hands or faces.",
  "signature": "The oversized open straight razor, drawn in fine steel lines and slicing diagonally off the right edge of the dark hero beside the huge Garamond headline, with faint steam rising above it.",
  "copy": {
    "headline": "Britev, vroča brisača in miren stol v starem Mariboru",
    "lead": "Luka Kos se je brivske obrti učil v Zagrebu in na Dunaju. Na Poštni ulici vas postriže s škarjami ali strojčkom, uredi brado in obrije z britvijo."
  },
  "imagePrompt": "One flat full-page screenshot of a desktop homepage, 1536x1024 px, with no browser window, no device frame and no perspective. This is the website of a classic men's barbershop in Maribor's old town. There are no photographs anywhere; the only imagery is fine ink line drawings. Fonts: EB Garamond for headings (large, regular weight, sentence case, elegant Viennese feel) and Karla for body text (small, plain). The page ground is deep green-black #14201d. Top bar: wordmark in EB Garamond #eeeae3 at left, phone number in Karla at right, and a thin #2f413c rule below. Hero: on the left seven columns, a huge three-line EB Garamond headline in #eeeae3 at about 10vw, then a short Karla lead in #9fb0ad, then one rectangular button with slightly square corners in oxblood #b23a2e with #f6f2ec text. On the right five columns, a large drawing of an open straight razor in thin pale steel lines (#9fb0ad and #eeeae3) on the plain dark ground, angled diagonally and bleeding off the right edge of the page, with three delicate steam curls above it; it contains no text, hands or people. Below the hero is a full-width oxblood #b23a2e ribbon holding one line of short words in EB Garamond #f6f2ec separated by small diamond marks. Next is a story section on very light cool tint #eef1f0 with dark ink #14201d text: a Garamond heading on the left, running Karla text on the right, and a small ink line drawing of a neatly folded hot towel with faint steam under the heading. Then a services section on #14201d: the heading on the left, and on the right a tall ruled list of service names in Garamond #eeeae3 with small Karla notes in #9fb0ad, separated by hairline #2f413c rules, with no prices. Then a full-width oxblood #b23a2e band: a heading and short text on the left, and on the right the phone number as a giant EB Garamond numeral in #f6f2ec. The last section is on #1c2b27: the address block, the opening hours as a seven-day week strip with thin dividers, and a simple schematic line map of old-town streets in #9fb0ad with one small oxblood dot. Use asymmetric left-aligned layouts throughout, with nothing centred, no gradients, no shadows, no icons and no pill shapes."
}

